hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"325","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: The two months of 'Id (festival), Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah, are not defective. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2323)"
"326","I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Allah Almighty will continuously plant (new) plants in this religion, and He will continue to use those people for His obedience."
"327","There is no god but Allah; there is a destruction in store for Arabia because of the turmoil which is near at hand as the barrier of Gog and Magog has been opened like it, and he (in order to explain it) made a ring with the help of his thumb and forefinger. I said: Messenger of Allah, would we be destroyed despite the fact that there would be pious people amongst us? He said: Yes, when evil would be predominant. (Using translation from Muslim 2880c)"
"328","I will cast him into Hell. And whoever comes near to Me by a handspan, I come near to him by an arm's length; and whoever comes near to Me by an arm's length, I come near to him by the span of two outstretched arms. And whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him running; and whoever comes to Me running, I come to him even more swiftly. And whoever remembers Me in his heart, I remember him alone; and whoever remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better and purer than his."
"329","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have accepted Islam as a reward for the deeds you did before."
"330","The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! Because he never said: O Allah! Forgive my sins on the Day of Resurrection."
"331","I asked: O Messenger of Allah! Ibn Jud'an used to maintain ties of kinship and feed people during the time of ignorance, will this benefit him? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: No, it will not benefit him, because he never said: O my Lord! Forgive my sins."
"332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Your father was seeking something and he attained it,” (the narrator says) meaning fame. Sayyiduna ‘Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I want to ask you about such food which I sometimes leave out of caution?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not leave anything in which Christianity has participated.” Sayyiduna ‘Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said, “I release my dog and then it catches a prey, but I do not find anything with which to slaughter it, except a knife or a stick.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Spill the blood with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah (and then eat the prey).”"
"333","that it was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Are the people of Jannah ˹already˺ known from the people of Hellfire? He said, then he (the Prophet) said: ""Yes."" He said, it was again said: Then what is the use of ˹anyone˺ doing ˹any˺ deeds? He (the Prophet) said: ""Everyone is facilitated toward what has been created for him."" (Using translation from Muslim 2649a)"
"334","We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ at a funeral - I [the narrator] think he said in Baqeeʿ al-Gharqad - and he struck the ground (with a stick), then he lifted his head and said: “There is no one among you but Allah has decreed his place in Paradise or his place in Hell.” We said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, shouldnʿt we rely on that? He said: ʿNo, rather strive, for each will be enabled [to do the appropriate deeds].” Then he recited: ʿAs for him who gives (in charity) and keeps his duty to Allah and fears Him, And believes in Al-Husna.ʿ We will make smooth for him the path of ease (goodness). But he who is greedy miser and thinks himself self sufficient. And belies Al-Husna. We will make smooth for him the path for evil” [Al-Lail 92:5-10]. (Al-Husna: The Best (i.e. either La ilaha illAllaah: none has the right to be worshipped but Allah) or a reward from Allah (i.e. Allah will compensate him for what he will spend in Allahʿs way or bless him with Paradise) Footnote from Hilali/Khan Translation of meanings) (Using translation from Aḥmad 1110)"
"335","We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ at a funeral - I [the narrator] think he said in Baqeeʿ al-Gharqad - and he struck the ground (with a stick), then he lifted his head and said: “There is no one among you but Allah has decreed his place in Paradise or his place in Hell.” We said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, shouldnʿt we rely on that? He said: ʿNo, rather strive, for each will be enabled [to do the appropriate deeds].” Then he recited: ʿAs for him who gives (in charity) and keeps his duty to Allah and fears Him, And believes in Al-Husna.ʿ We will make smooth for him the path of ease (goodness). But he who is greedy miser and thinks himself self sufficient. And belies Al-Husna. We will make smooth for him the path for evil” [Al-Lail 92:5-10]. (Al-Husna: The Best (i.e. either La ilaha illAllaah: none has the right to be worshipped but Allah) or a reward from Allah (i.e. Allah will compensate him for what he will spend in Allahʿs way or bless him with Paradise) Footnote from Hilali/Khan Translation of meanings) (Using translation from Aḥmad 1110)"
"336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is a situation that has already been decreed."" So Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""Then why should one act?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every doer, his specific action has been made easy."
"337","I will always strive my utmost regarding actions."
"338","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the basis of the decree of destiny."
"339","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Deeds are like vessels. If the lower part is good then the upper part will be good, and if the lower part is bad then the upper part will be bad.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4199)"
"340","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The outcome of deeds depends upon their ending."
"341","""When Allah wants good for a slave, He puts him in action."" It was said: ""How does he put him in action O Messenger Of Allah?"" He said: ""By making him meet up with the righteous deeds before death."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2142)"
"342","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He purifies him before his death (that is, He makes his praiseworthy qualities known)."" It was asked: What is meant by purifying him before his death? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Righteous deeds are opened up for him before his death, until that person becomes pleased with them."
"343","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He makes him pure (i.e., He grants him a good reputation) before his death."" It was asked: What is meant by making him pure? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before his death, righteous deeds are opened up for him, until that person becomes pleased with them."
"344","The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: When we are with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), we find our inner states to be pleasing, but when we go to our families and mingle with them, our states become different. The noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: If you were to remain permanently in the state you are in when you are with me, then the angels would shake hands with you and shade you with their wings, but (the state) changes from time to time."
"345","“If the believer knew what is with Allah of punishment, none would hope for Paradise, and if the disbeliever knew what is with Allah of mercy, none would despair of (attaining) Paradise.” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3542)"
"346","Sahl b. Sa'd reported it from Messenger of Allah ﷺ that a person performs deeds like the deeds of the people of Paradise apparently before people and he would be amongst the dwellers of Hell and a person acts apparently like the people of Hell, but (in fact) he would be among the dwellers of Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 112b)"
"347","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Allah said, 'I will declare war against him who shows hostility to a pious worshipper of Mine. And the most beloved things with which My slave comes nearer to Me, is what I have enjoined upon him; and My slave keeps on coming closer to Me through performing Nawafil (praying or doing extra deeds besides what is obligatory) till I love him, so I become his sense of hearing with which he hears, and his sense of sight with which he sees, and his hand with which he grips, and his leg with which he walks; and if he asks Me, I will give him, and if he asks My protection (Refuge), I will protect him; (i.e. give him My Refuge) and I do not hesitate to do anything as I hesitate to take the soul of the believer, for he hates death, and I hate to disappoint him."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6502)"
"348","“Be moderate and adhere to moderation, for there is no one among you who will be saved by his deeds.” They said: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Not even me. Unless Allah encompasses me with mercy and grace from Him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4201)"
"349","""Indeed for everything there is a zeal, and for every zeal there is a slackening. So if its practitioner behaves properly,and is moderate, then hope for him (for his success). But if the fingers are pointed to him, then do not count him (among the worthy)."" It has been related from Anas bin Malik that the Prophet SAW said: ""It is sufficient evil for a man that fingers be raised against him, regarding religion or worldly matters, except for one whom Allah has protected."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2453)"
"350","“Be moderate and adhere to moderation, for there is no one among you who will be saved by his deeds.” They said: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Not even me. Unless Allah encompasses me with mercy and grace from Him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4201)"
"351","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Indeed, this religion is easy, and no one will ever overburden himself in religion, except that it will overcome him. So seek what is appropriate, and come as close as you can, and receive the glad tidings (that you will be rewarded), and take it easy; and gain strength by worshipping in the mornings, afternoons, and during the last hours of the nights.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5034)"
"352","""I will certainly stand all night (in prayer) and fast every day for as long as I live."" The Messenger of Allah said: ""Are you the one who said that?"" I said: 'I said it, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah said: 'You cannot do that. Fast and break your fast, sleep and stand (in prayer), and fast three days of each month. For a good deed is equal to ten like it, and that is like fasting for a lifetime.' I said: 'But I am able to do bette than that.' He said: 'Fast for one day and break your fast for two days.' I said: 'I am able to do better than that, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Then fast for one day and break your fast for two days.' I said: 'I am able to do better than that, O Messenger of Allah said : 'There is noting better than that.""' 'Abdullah said: ""If I had accepted the three days that the Messenger of Allah said, that would be dearer to me than my family and my wealth."" 'Ata said: ""someone who heard him told me that Ibn 'Umar (said) that the Prophet said: 'Whoever fasts every day of his life, then he has not fasted."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2392)"
"353","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do as much (good) deeds as you are able, for Allah’s bounty will not be cut off from you until you become weary.” Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The most beloved deed to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was that which was done regularly, even if it was little. Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed any (supererogatory) prayer, he would perform it regularly. The narrator states: Allah Almighty has said: “And those who regularly perform their prayers.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): “Indeed, Allah does not tire until you tire.” This is among the expressions of the people’s idiom, because the meaning can only be conveyed to the addressed person in this way. Its real meaning is not intended."
"354","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty likes that His concession be accepted, just as He likes that His obligatory commands be acted upon."
"355","the Messenger of Allah passed by a man in the shade of a tree on whom water was being sprinkled. He said: ""What is the matter with your companion?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, he is fasting."" He said: ""It is not righteousness to fast when traveling. Take to the concession which Allah has granted you, accept it."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2258)"
"356","narrates: After the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) arrived in Madinah Munawwarah, he never fasted for a whole month except during Ramadan. He (peace be upon him) would only fast for the entire month in Ramadan."
"357","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who was praying on a rock, and he went towards Makkah and stayed a while, then he left and found the man still praying as he had been. He stood up and clasped his hands, then said: “O people, you should observe moderation,” three times, “for Allah does not get tired (of giving reward) but you get tired.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4241)"
"358","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""If you knew that which I know, you would laugh little and weep much."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6486)"
"359","The grace of Allah does not cease from you until you become weary."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Allah does not tire until you tire,"" these are words of common parlance used by people to convey the meaning to the listener, and that meaning can only be conveyed through these words."
"360","Uthman was sitting in alMaqaʿid. He called for water and did wudoo’, then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing wudooʿ in this place where I am sitting then he said: “whoever does wudoo’ as I have done, then gets up and prays two rakʿahs, his previous sins will be forgiven.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿDo not become complacent.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 478)"
"361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is a good deed that has been placed (for you). (Now it is up to you) whether you gain much or little from it. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Which deed is the most virtuous? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: To have faith in Allah and to strive in the path of Allah. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Who among the believers is the most complete in faith? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one with the best character. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Who among the believers is the safest (from whose harm others are safe)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one from whose tongue and hand people are safe. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Which prayer is the most virtuous? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one in which the standing (qiyam) is long. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Which migration (hijrah) is the most virtuous? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one who abandons sins. I said: O Messenger of Allah! What is fasting? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is an obligation, which suffices, and with Allah its reward is multiplied many times. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Which jihad is the most virtuous? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one in which the (horse’s) legs are cut and its blood is shed. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Which charity is the most virtuous? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one given by a person who has little wealth and fears becoming poor. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Of all that Allah has revealed to you, what is the greatest thing? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Ayat al-Kursi. Then he said: In comparison to Allah’s Kursi, the seven heavens are like a ring placed on a barren land, and the ‘Arsh has the same superiority over the Kursi as that land has over the ring. I said: O Messenger of Allah! How many prophets are there? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: One hundred and twenty thousand. I said: How many of them are messengers? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Three hundred and thirteen. I said: Who was the first among them? He said: Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah! Was he a prophet and a messenger? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. Allah created him with His own hand of power, breathed into him of His spirit, and spoke to him directly. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr! Four of them were Syriac: Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Sheeth (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Akhnukh (peace be upon him)—that is, Sayyiduna Idris (peace be upon him), and he was the first to write with a pen—and Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him). Four were Arabs: Sayyiduna Hud (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Shu‘ayb (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Salih (peace be upon him), and your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah! How many books has Allah revealed? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: One hundred and four books. Fifty scrolls were revealed to Sayyiduna Sheeth (peace be upon him), thirty scrolls to Sayyiduna Akhnukh (peace be upon him), ten scrolls to Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him), ten scrolls to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) before the Torah, then the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and the Qur’an were revealed. I said: O Messenger of Allah! What was in the scripture of Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It was all parables, but it was written in it: “O king! To whom sovereignty has been given, and who is tested and deceived, I did not send you so that you gather the world against each other. I sent you so that you do not let the supplication of the oppressed reach Me, for I do not reject the supplication of the oppressed, even if he is a disbeliever. And it is incumbent upon the wise person, as long as his intellect is not overcome, to divide his time into portions: some time for supplication to his Lord, some time for self-accounting, some time for reflection on the creation of Allah, and some time for preparing food and drink. It is incumbent upon the wise person to prepare for three things: provision for his end (i.e., the Hereafter), necessities for his life, or a pleasure that is not forbidden. And it is incumbent upon the wise person to have insight into his era, to pay attention to his present, to guard his tongue, and whoever accounts for his speech more than his deeds, his speech will be little, and only that which is necessary.” I said: O Messenger of Allah! What was in the scripture of Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It was all admonitions. (Some of them are:) “I am amazed at the one who believes in death, yet is happy. I am amazed at the one who believes in Hell, yet laughs. I am amazed at the one who believes in destiny, yet strives (for the world). I am amazed at the one who sees the changing conditions of the world and its people, yet is content with the world. I am amazed at the one who believes in reckoning, yet does not act.” I said: O Messenger of Allah! Advise me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I advise you to fear Allah, for it is the foundation of all matters. I said: O Messenger of Allah! More. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You must recite the Qur’an and remember Allah, for it will be a light for you on earth and a treasure for you in the Hereafter. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me more. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You must avoid excessive laughter, for it deadens the heart and removes the light from the face. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me more. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You must observe silence, except in speaking good, for it will drive the devil away from you and help you in your religious matters. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me more. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You must strive in jihad, for it is the monasticism of my Ummah. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me more. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Look to those below you, not to those above you, for this will prevent you from belittling the blessings of Allah upon you. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me more. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Speak the truth, even if it is bitter. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me more. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Let that which you know about yourself keep you away from people, and do not harbor feelings against people for what you do yourself. It is enough of a fault for you to recognize in people what you are unaware of in yourself, or to harbor feelings against people for what you do yourself. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) struck his blessed hand on my chest and said: “O Abu Dharr! There is no wisdom like planning, no abstinence like refraining, and no nobility like good character.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator Abu Idris al-Khawlani is ‘A’idh Allah ibn ‘Abdullah. He was born in the year of the Battle of Hunayn during the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and died in Syria in the year 80 AH. The narrator Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani was from Kindah and lived in Damascus. He was among the experts of fiqh and Qur’an recitation in Syria. He heard hadith from Abu Idris al-Khawlani at the age of fifteen. He was born on the day of Rahat during the caliphate of Mu‘awiyah ibn Yazid in 64 AH. Sulayman ibn ‘Abd al-Malik appointed him as the judge of Mosul. He heard hadith from Sa‘id ibn al-Musayyib and the people of Hijaz. He remained in the position of judge there until ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Aziz became caliph, then the ruler kept him in office, and he continued in that position throughout his reign. He lived a long life until he died in Damascus in 133 AH."",""He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah"",""how many prophets were there? He said: *""""One hundred and twenty thousand.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" how many messengers were among them? He said: *""""Three hundred and thirteen"","" a great multitude.""""* He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" who was the first of them? He said: *""""Adam.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" was he a prophet sent as a messenger? He said: *""""Yes. Allah created him with His hand"","" breathed into him of His spirit"","" and spoke to him directly.""""* Then he said: *""""O Abu Dharr"","" four were Syriac: Adam"","" Sheeth"","" Akhnukh—who is Idris and was the first to write with the pen—and Nuh; and four were Arabs: Hud"","" Shuayb"","" Salih"","" and your prophet Muhammad ﷺ.""""*"",""I said: O Messenger of Allah"",""how many books did Allah send down? He said: *""""One hundred books and four books: fifty scrolls were sent down to Sheeth"","" thirty scrolls were sent down to Akhnukh"","" ten scrolls were sent down to Ibrahim"","" ten scrolls were sent down to Musa before the Tawrah"","" and the Tawrah"","" the Injil"","" the Zabur"","" and the Quran were sent down.""""* He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" what was in the scroll of Ibrahim? He said: *""""It was all parables: O empowered king"","" afflicted and deluded"","" I did not send you to pile up this world"","" one part upon another; rather"","" I sent you to turn back from Me the supplication of the oppressed"","" for I do not reject it even if it comes from a disbeliever. The intelligent person"","" so long as his mind is not overcome"","" should have periods: a period in which he privately calls upon his Lord; a period in which he takes himself to account; a period in which he reflects on the work of Allah; and a period in which he withdraws for his needs of food and drink. The intelligent person should not set out except for three things: provision for the return"","" repair of livelihood"","" or pleasure that is not unlawful. The intelligent person should be aware of his time"","" attentive to his own affair"","" and guarding his tongue. Whoever counts his speech as part of his deeds"","" his speech will be little except in what concerns him.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" what was in the scrolls of Musa? He said: *""""They were all lessons: I am amazed at one who is certain of death"","" yet he rejoices; I am amazed at one who is certain of the Fire"","" yet he laughs; I am amazed at one who is certain of divine decree"","" yet he exhausts himself; I am amazed at one who sees the world and how it turns upon its people"","" yet he feels secure with it; and I am amazed at one who is certain of the reckoning tomorrow"","" yet does not act.""""*"",""I said: O Messenger of Allah"",""counsel me. He said: *""""I counsel you to fear Allah"","" for it is the head of the whole matter.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Hold fast to reciting the Quran and remembering Allah"","" for it is a light for you on earth and a treasure for you in heaven.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Beware of excessive laughter"","" for it kills the heart and takes away the light of the face.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Hold fast to silence except from good"","" for it drives Satan away from you and is a help for you in the matter of your religion.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Hold fast to jihad"","" for it is the monasticism of my community.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Love the poor and sit with them.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Look to those beneath you and do not look to those above you"","" for that is more likely that you will not look down upon Allah's blessing with you.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Speak the truth"","" even if it is bitter.""""* I said: O Messenger of Allah"","" give me more. He said: *""""Let what you know of yourself restrain you from people"","" and do not find fault with them for what you yourself do. It is enough as a fault in you that you recognize in people what you are ignorant of in yourself"","" or that you find fault with them for what you yourself do.""""* Then he struck my chest with his hand and said: *""""O Abu Dharr"","" there is no intelligence like careful planning"","" no piety like restraint"","" and no nobility like good character.""""*"""""
"362","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Do you know what is Allah's right upon His servants? I replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued for a while, then he said: Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah when they do that? I replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of the servants upon Allah is that when they do that, Allah will not punish them."
"363","""The Messenger of Allah said: Allah, the Most High, said: If My slave loves to meet Me, I love to meet him, and if he hates to meet Me, I hate to meet him.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1835)"
"364","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then acceptance is placed for that person on the earth. And when Allah the Exalted dislikes a servant, then the same happens in that manner."
"365","I love such and such person, so you also love him. Then Sayyiduna Jibreel, peace be upon him, also begins to love him. Then he announces among the inhabitants of the heavens: Indeed, Allah Almighty loves such and such person, so you all should also love him. Then the inhabitants of the heavens also begin to love him, and then acceptance is placed for that person on the earth."" And when Allah Almighty dislikes a servant—Malik, the narrator, said: I think the words 'dislikes' are in the narration—then the rest of the hadith is as previously mentioned. Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: This narration has been transmitted by Suhail from his father, and he has transmitted this narration from Qaqa’ bin Hakeem from his father."
"366","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is the glad tidings that a believer receives quickly."
"367","It was said to Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What is your opinion about the person who has done good deeds and the people praise him? He said: It is glad tidings for a believer (which he has received in this mortal world). (Using translation from Muslim 2642a)"
"368","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty loves a servant, He praises him with seven thousand virtues which that servant has not even committed, and when He is displeased with a servant, He mentions him with seven thousand evils which that person has not committed."
"369","Allah the Exalted and Glorious, said: I have prepared for My pious servants which no eye has ever seen, and no ear has ever heard, and no human heart has ever perceived but it is testified by the Book of Allah. He then recited:"" No soul knows what comfort has been concealed from them, as a reward for what they did"". (xxxii. 17) (Using translation from Muslim 2824a)"
"370","The command of Allah Almighty is) ""Indeed, We have given you a clear victory, so that Allah may forgive you your past and future sins."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) states: This verse was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) upon his return from Hudaybiyyah. The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were facing distress and sorrow. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A verse has been revealed to me which is more beloved to me than the world and all that is in it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse before the people. The people said: O Messenger of Allah! Allah Almighty has stated what He has done for you, but what will He do for us? (This has not been mentioned.) So Allah Almighty then revealed the following verse: ""So that He may admit the believing men and believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow."
"371","The command of Allah Almighty is:) ""Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory."" This verse was revealed to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) on the occasion of returning from Hudaybiyyah, when his companions were facing grief and hardship, because they had not achieved their objective and had sacrificed their sacrificial animals right there at Hudaybiyyah. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A verse has been revealed to me which is more beloved to me than the entire world."" Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this entire verse before those people. So one of those present said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Congratulations to you. Allah Almighty has made clear what He will do with you, but what will He do with us?"" Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""So that He may admit the believing men and believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow."
"372","narrates from Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal that the Prophet Muhammad said: ""Whoever strives in the path of Allah, he is under Allah's responsibility; and whoever visits a sick person, he is also under Allah's responsibility; and whoever goes to the mosque in the morning or evening, he is under Allah's responsibility; and whoever goes to the ruler of the time in order to help him, he is also under Allah's responsibility; and whoever stays in his house and does not backbite any person, he is also under Allah's responsibility (i.e., he is in His protection)."
"373","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""He should give a little from the sustenance Allah has given him (in the way of Allah)."" I said, ""What if he is a person who has nothing?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""He should say a good word with his tongue."" I said, ""What if he is so incapacitated that he cannot say anything with his tongue?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""He should help an overpowered person."" I said, ""What if he is so weak that he cannot even do that?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then he should do some work for a disabled person."" I said, ""What if he himself is disabled?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards me and said, ""If you do not want to leave any good remaining for this person, then he should keep people safe from his harm."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Are these words for the sake of making things easy?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul, whoever among the servants does any of these deeds and seeks reward from Allah through it, then this deed will take him by the hand on the Day of Resurrection and admit him into Paradise."" Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: Abu Kathir Suhaimi's name is Yazid bin Abdur Rahman Udhaynah, and he was from Yamamah and among the trustworthy narrators."",""He said"",""""""I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that"","" and he said"","" 'He believes in Allah.'"""""",""I said"",""""""O Messenger of Allah"","" is there any other deed alongside faith?"""""",""He said"",""""""He is content with what Allah has provided for him."""""",""I said"",""""""Even if he is deprived of everything?"""""",""He said"",""""""He speaks good words with his tongue."""""",""I said"",""""""What if he is mute and cannot speak?"""""",""He said"",""""""He helps the oppressed."""""",""I said"",""""""What if he is weak and has no strength?"""""",""He said"",""""""Then let him support the disabled."""""",""I said"",""""""What if he himself is disabled?"""""",""He looked at me and said"",""""""If you want to leave your friend with some good"","" then do not harm others."""""",""I said"",""""""O Messenger of Allah"","" is this a word of ease?"""""",""He ﷺ  said"",""""""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! No servant performs a quality from these qualities"","" desiring with it what is with Allah"","" except that it will take hold of him on the Day of Resurrection until it brings him into Paradise."""""""""
"374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have used few words but asked about a great matter. Free a soul (i.e., a slave man or woman) and set a neck free. He asked: Are these not the same thing? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, freeing a soul means that you simply set him free, and setting a neck free means that you pay his price (and free another person’s slave). Give such a gift that continues (to benefit), and spend on a relative who does not maintain ties of kinship. And if you do not have the ability for this, then feed the hungry, give drink to the thirsty, enjoin good, and forbid evil. And if you do not have the ability for even this, then restrain your tongue except for good words."
"375","“A man said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, I do a good deed, then others find out about it and that pleases me.’ He said: ‘You will have two rewards, the reward for doing it in secret and the reward for doing it openly (so that others may follow your example).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4226)"
"376","I draw near to him by a cubit; and when he draws near to Me by a cubit, I draw near to him by a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I go to him running; and if he comes to Me running, I go to him even more swiftly. And Allah Almighty is Most Forgiving, Most Merciful.”"
"377","Verily, Allah does not treat a believer unjustly in regard to his virtues. He would confer upon him (His blessing) in this world and would give him reward in the Hereafter. And as regards a non-believer, he would be made to taste the reward (of virtue in this world) what he has done for himself so much that when it would be the Hereafter, he would find no virtue for which he should be rewarded. (Using translation from Muslim 2808a)"
"378","I go down and remember Allah Almighty, I will attain more goodness.’ Then he came down from there, and with him was one or perhaps two loaves of bread. As soon as he reached the land, he met a woman. The monk began to talk to this woman, and she began to talk to him, until he committed adultery with her. Then, when he was overcome with remorse, he went down into a well to bathe. Meanwhile, a beggar came to him, so he gestured with his hand for him to take those two loaves, or one loaf. Then the monk died, and his sixty years of worship were weighed against that one act of adultery, and the adultery outweighed his good deeds. Then the one or two loaves were placed with his good deeds, and the scale of his good deeds became heavier, and the man was forgiven.” Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: This narration was heard by the narrator Ghalib bin Wazir from the narrator Waki’ in Bayt al-Maqdis. He did not narrate this in Iraq. This is one of those narrations which the people of Palestine uniquely narrate from Waki’."
"379","I record one good deed for him as long as he does not do it. When he acts upon it, I record it as tenfold reward. And when the servant thinks of committing a sin, I forgive him as long as he does not commit it. But when he commits it, I record it as one sin."
"380","narrates: He learned of this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): “Allah Almighty (says to the angels), when My servant intends to do a good deed, then record it as one good deed, and when he acts upon it, then record it as tenfold. And when My servant intends to do an evil deed, then do not record it, and if he refrains from it, then record it as one good deed.”"
"381","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""(O angels!) When My servant intends to commit an evil deed and does not act upon it, then you record it as a good deed, and if he acts upon it, then you record it as an evil deed, and if he repents from it, then you erase the evil from his record. And when My servant intends to do a good deed and does not act upon it, then you record it as a good deed, and if he acts upon it, then you record it as a reward from ten times up to seven hundred times."
"382","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah the Exalted says: (O angels!) When My servant intends to commit an evil deed, do not record it until he acts upon it. If he does act upon it, then record it as one evil deed. If he leaves it for My sake, then record it as one good deed. If he intends to do a good deed, then record it as a good deed. If he also acts upon that good deed, then record it as tenfold up to seven hundredfold (reward and recompense).”"
"383","The reason is: the ultimate point of “ham” is resolve, and the Arabs, in their idiom, apply the name of the beginning to the end, and the name of the end to the beginning. The reason is: mere intention is not written in a person’s record of deeds, because it is only a thought and has no ruling. And there is also the possibility in this that, whoever intends to do a good deed, Allah Almighty writes a good deed for him even if he has not firmly resolved and has not acted upon it. Allah Almighty may do so due to the virtue of Islam, so Allah Almighty granting a servant the ability to accept Islam is a favor He has done upon His servant, and recording the good deed for the servant who intends a good deed but does not act upon it is also Allah Almighty’s favor. And if a servant intends an evil deed and does not act upon it, then if Allah Almighty records it, it would be according to justice. But, because His favor surpasses His justice, and thus His mercy has overtaken His wrath, so it is included in His favor and mercy that the sins of Muslim children are not recorded until they reach puberty, and their good deeds are recorded. So it will be like this, and there is no difference in it."
"384","I record one good deed for him. If he acts upon it, I record for him from ten to seven hundred times as much. If he intends to do an evil deed and does not act upon it, I do not record anything against him. If he acts upon it, I record one evil deed against him."
"385","I asked AbuTha'labah al-Khushani: What is your opinion about the verse ""Care for yourselves"". He said: I swear by Allah, I asked the one who was well informed about it; I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. He said: No, enjoin one another to do what is good and forbid one another to do what is evil. But when you see niggardliness being obeyed, passion being followed, worldly interests being preferred, everyone being charmed with his opinion, then care for yourself, and leave alone what people in general are doing; for ahead of you are days which will require endurance, in which showing endurance will be like grasping live coals. The one who acts rightly during that period will have the reward of fifty men who act as he does. Another version has: He said (The hearers asked:) Messenger of Allah, the reward of fifty of them? He replied: The reward of fifty of you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4341)"
"386","A prostitute saw a dog moving around a well on a hot day and hanging out its tongue because of thirst. She drew water for it in her shoe and she was pardoned (for this act of hers). (Using translation from Muslim 2245a)"
"387","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) says: Dhul-Kifl felt remorse, and he stood up without doing anything. That very night, he died. In the morning, it was written on his door: 'Indeed, Allah the Exalted has forgiven you.'"
"388","‘Umar bin Al Khattab reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “Actions are to be judged only by intentions and a man will have only what he intended. When one’s emigration is to Allaah and His Apostle, his emigration is to Allaah and His Apostle but his emigration is to a worldly end at which he aims or to a woman whom he marries , his emigration is to that for which he emigrated. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2201)"
"389","‘Umar bin Al Khattab reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “Actions are to be judged only by intentions and a man will have only what he intended. When one’s emigration is to Allaah and His Apostle, his emigration is to Allaah and His Apostle but his emigration is to a worldly end at which he aims or to a woman whom he marries , his emigration is to that for which he emigrated. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2201)"
"390","The second said: If He can hear when we speak loudly, then He should certainly hear when we speak softly as well. The third said: I think that Allah Almighty hears everything we say. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him about what those people had said, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""And whatever you conceal, your hearing and your sight will bear witness against you."
"391","The second said: If we speak loudly, He will hear it; if we speak in a low voice, He will not hear it. The third said: If He can hear loud speech, then He can also hear low speech. (Sayyiduna Abdullah says) I went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this matter before him, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse: “And whatever you conceal, your hearing, your sight, and your skins will bear witness against you.”"
"392","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Deeds are like vessels. If the lower part is good then the upper part will be good, and if the lower part is bad then the upper part will be bad.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4199)"
"393","I will fill your chest with contentment and remove your poverty. But if you do not do so, I will fill your hands with occupations and will not remove your poverty."
"394","Verily Allah does not look to your faces and your wealth but He looks to your heart and to your deeds. (Using translation from Muslim 2564c)"
"395","I am the most independent of all partners. Whoever does a deed and associates someone else with Me in it, I am free from that deed; it is for the one whom he associated with Me."
"396","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Whoever does good in Islam, he will not be held accountable for what he did during the time of ignorance. And whoever does evil in Islam, then he will be held accountable for all his deeds, both former and later."
"397","I asked Messenger of Allah ﷺ about virtue and vice. He said: Virtue is a kind disposition and vice is what rankles in your heart and that you disapprove that people should come to know of it. (Using translation from Muslim 2553a)"
"398","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Allah Almighty will surely mention in this world a people who will be upon adorned beds, and He will surely admit them to elevated ranks."
"399","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""A Muslim is the one who avoids harming Muslims with his tongue and hands. And a Muhajir (emigrant) is the one who gives up (abandons) all what Allah has forbidden."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 10)"
"400","Verily a person asked the Messenger of Allah (may peace and blessings be upon him) who amongst the Muslims was better. Upon this (the Holy Prophet) remarked: From whose hand and tongue the Muslims are safe. (Using translation from Muslim 40)"
"401","""There was a woman who performed Salat behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who was the most beautiful among the people. Some of the people would go forward to the first line so as not to see her. Others would go back to the last line so when he would bow, he could look at her from under his armpit. So Allah revealed: Indeed We know those who try to come forward among you, and We know those who try to go back (15:24). (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3122)"
"402","I guide you to something that erases sins?"" The people said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Performing ablution well when the self is reluctant (here, the narrator is unsure whether the word used was 'ablution' or 'purification'), walking more steps towards the mosque, and performing one prayer after another prayer. Whoever performs ablution well, leaves his house, and comes to the mosque, and (the narrator is unsure, perhaps) prays with the Muslims following the Imam, and then waits for the next prayer after it, the angels say: 'O Allah! Forgive him. O Allah! Have mercy on him.' When you stand for prayer, straighten your rows and fill the gaps in between. When the Imam says the takbir, you also say the takbir, for I can see you even from behind me. When the Imam « » says, you say « » . The best row for men is the front row, and the least good row for men is the last row. The best row for women is the last row, and the least good row for women is the front row. O group of women! When the men go into prostration, protect your gaze regarding the private parts of the men."" The narrator says: I asked Abdullah bin Abu Bakr: What does this mean? (i.e., what is the reason for this instruction), so he said: Because their lower garments used to be short."
"403","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That which Allah Almighty does not like from you, do not do it even in seclusion."
"404","""My father informed me, from Ibn Mina, from ABu Sa'eed bin Abi Fadalah Al-Ansari - and he was one of the Companions - who said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When Allah gathers the people on the Day of Judgement - a Day in which there is no doubt in - a caller will call out: 'Whoever committed Shirk in any of his deeds he did for Allah - then let him seek his reward from other than Allah. For indeed Allah is the most free of the partners from any need of Shirk."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3154)"
"405","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Give glad tidings to this Ummah of help, brilliance, and establishment (i.e., influence in the world). Whoever among them performs an act of the Hereafter for the sake of the world will have no share in the Hereafter."
"406","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said this: I had not heard anyone else saying that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said this, so I moved closer to Sayyiduna Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him). I heard him saying that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever acts for fame, Allah will make his fame known, and whoever acts for show, Allah will make his show apparent."
"407","“Whoever wants to be heard of, Allah will make him heard of, and whoever wants to be seen, Allah will show him (i.e., expose his real motives).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4207)"
"408",""" Who is this?"" They said: ""Abu Hurairah."" (He said):So I got close to him until I was sitting in front of him as he was narrating to the people. When he was silent and alone, I said to him: "" I ask youabsolute truth if you would narrate to me a Hadith which you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, That you understand and know."" So Abu Hurairah said: ""You want me to narrate a Hadith to you which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me that I understand and know."" Then Abu Hurairah began sobbing profusely. We sat for a while, then he recovered and said: ""I shall narrate to you a Hadith which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated in this House, while there was no one with us other than he and I."" Then, again, Abu Hurairah began sobbing severely. Then he recovered, and wiped his face, and said: ""you want me to narrate to you a Hadith which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated while he and I were sitting in this House, and no one was with us but he and I."" Then Abu Hurairah began sobbing severely. Then he bent, falling on his face, so I supported him for a long time."",""Then he recovered and said: """"The Messenger of Allah narrated to me that on the Day of Judgement"",""Allah"","" Most High"","" will descend to His slaves t judge between them. Every nation shall be kneeling. The first of those who will be called before him will be a man who memorized the Qur'an"","" and a man who was killed in Allah's cause"","" and a wealthy man. Allah will say to the reciter: 'Did I not teach you what I revealed to My Messenger?"""" He says: 'Of course O Lord!' He says: 'Then what did you do with what you learned?' He said: 'I would stand (in prayer reciting) with it during all hours of the night and all hours of the day.' Then Allah would say to him: 'You have lied.' And the angels will say: 'You have lied.'Allah will say to him: 'Rather"","" you wanted it to be said that so-and-so is a reciter. And that was said.' The person with the wealth will be brought"","" and Allah will say to him: 'Was I not so generous with you"","" such that I did not leave you having any need from anyone?' He will say: 'Of course O Lord!' He says: 'Then what did you do with what I gave to you?' He says: 'I would nurture the ties of kinship and give charity.' Then Allah will say to him: 'You have lied.' And the angels will say to him: 'You have lied.' Allah"","" Most High"","" will say: 'Rather"","" you wanted it to be said that so-and-so is so generous"","" and that was said.' Then the one who was killed in Allah's cause shall be brought"","" and Allah will say to him : 'For what were you killed?' So he says: 'I was commanded to fight in Your cause "",""so I fought until I was killed.' Allah [Most High] will say to him: 'You have lied.' And the angels will say to him: 'You have lied.' Allah [Most High] will say: 'Rather"","" you wanted it be said that so-and-so is brave"","" and that was said.' "",""Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hit me on my knees and said: 'O Abu Hurairah! These first three are the creatures of Allah with whom the fire will be enflamed on the Day of Judgement.'"" ,""Al-Walid Abu 'Uthman Al-Mada'ini said: """"So 'Uqbah bin Muslim informed me that Shaufaiy"",""is the one who entered upon Mu'awiyah to inform him about this."""" Abu Uthman said: 'This has been done with these people"","" then how about with those who remain among the people?"""" Then Mu'awiyah begin weeping so intensely"","" that we thought that he will kill himself with excessive weeping. We said: """"This man came to us to cause evil."""" Then Mu'awiyah recovered"","" wiped off his face and said: """"Allah and His Messenger told the truth: Whosoever desires the life of the world and its glitter"","" then we shall pay in full (the wages of) their deeds therein"","" and they shall have no diminution therein. They are those for whom there is nothing in the Hereafter Fire"","" and vain are the deeds they did therein. And of no effect is that which they used to do."""" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2382)"""""
"409","The reason is: When Jibreel (peace be upon him) said to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever finds the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance him from His forgiveness,"" the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) immediately said: Ameen. Similarly, when Jibreel (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds his parents, or one of them, and enters Hell, may Allah distance him from His mercy,"" (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, immediately said Ameen). But when Jibreel (peace be upon him) said in your presence: ""Whoever, in whose presence your mention is made, and he does not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance him (from His mercy),"" the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not immediately say Ameen, because in this sentence there was a reference to his own self. Until Jibreel (peace be upon him) requested him to say Ameen, then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I said Ameen. The intention of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in this was to establish an example in this matter that one should not seek help from others for his own self, because Allah is the Helper of His friends in this world and the Hereafter, even if they dislike seeking help from people in this world."
"410","narrates: A man came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) who had quarreled with his father because of a debt that was obligatory upon his father. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""You and your wealth belong to your father."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: This means that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade this person from treating his father in the manner that is reserved for strangers, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) commanded him to do good to his father and to be gentle in speech and action, to the extent that he included his wealth with his father's, and he said to him: ""You and your wealth belong to your father."" But this does not mean that the father becomes the owner of the son's wealth while the son is alive and does not wish (that his father use his wealth without his consent)."
"411","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One of the major sins is that a person abuses his parents."" It was asked: How can a person abuse his parents? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He abuses the parents of others, so they abuse his parents."
"412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A man abuses another’s father, so he abuses his father in return. He abuses another’s mother, so he abuses his mother in return.”"
"413","I used to recite to ‘AbdurRahman bin ‘Awf, and he found me waiting for him. That was in Mina during the last Hajj performed by ʿUmar bin al-Khattab ؓ Abdur-Rahman bin ʿAwf said: A man came to ʿUmar bin al-Khattab and said: So and so is saying: If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I will swear allegiance to So and so. ʼUmar ؓ said: I will stand before the people today and warn them against these people who want to deprive them of their rights, ʿAbdur-Rahman said: I said: O Ameer al-Muʿmineen, do not do that, for the Hajj season brings together the riffraff and rabble among the people, and most of the people who gather around and listen to you will be of that type. Is you stand before the people, I am afraid that you will say something that they will spread and not understand it properly or interpret it properly. Rather wait until you come to Madinah, for it is the land of Hijrah and the Sunnah, and you will meet the most knowledgeable and noble people there, and you can say what you want to say with confidence; they wilt understand what you say and will interpret it correctly, ʿUmar ؓ said: If I reach Madinah safe and sound, I shall certainly talk to the people there in the first speech I deliver. When we came to Madinah at the end of Dhul-I-Iijah, it was a Friday. I set out early, ‘Umar did not care at what time he went out, because he did not pay attention to heat and cold and so on. I found Saʿeed bin Zaid at the right-hand corner of the minbar, he had got there before me. I sat down next to him, with my knee touching his knee, and it was not long before ʿUmar ؓ came. When I saw him, I said: He will certainly speak today on this minbar and say something that no one ever heard before. Saʿeed bin Zaid objected to that and said: What do you think he will say that no one said before? ʿUmar ؓ sat on the minbar, and when the muʿdhdhin fell silent, he stood up and praised and glorified Allah as He deserves, then he said: To proceed o people, I am going to tell you something that it has been decreed I should say. I do not know, perhaps it may signal my death. So whoever understands it and remembers it, let him narrate it to others wherever his mount takes him; whoever does not understand il, it is not permissible for him to tell lies about me. Allah, may He be blessed and exalted, sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth and revealed the Book to him; among the things that were revealed to him was the verse of stoning [adulterers). We read it and understood it; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned [adulterers] and we stoned adulterers] after him. But I fear that with the passage of time, some people will say: We do not find the verse of stoning in the Book of Allah, thus they will go astray by forsaking an obligation that Allah revealed. Stoning is the due punishment in the Book of Allah for those who commit zina, both men and women, if they have been married and if proof is established, or there is a pregnancy or a confession, And we used to recite: Do not claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, as it is disbelief (or ingratitude) on your part to claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, Verily the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿDo not praise me excessively as ʿEesa, the son of Maryam, was praised; rather I am the slave of Allah, so say, the slave of Allah and His Messenger.ʿ I have heard that some among you are saying. If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I shall swear allegiance to So and so. No man should deceive himself by saying that the oath of allegiance to Abu Bakr was given suddenly and it was is successful. There is no doubt that this is the case, but Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, saved the to 2 people from its bad consequences and there is no one among you today who has the qualities of Abu Bakr ؓ What happened to us when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died was that ‘Ali, az-Zubair and those who were with them stayed behind in the house of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and all the Ansar stayed behind and gathered in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, whilst the Muhajireen gathered around Abu Bakr ؓ I said to him; O Abu Bakr, let us go to our brothers, the Ansar. So we set out, looking for them, then we were met by two righteous men who told us what the people had done, and said: where are you going, O Muhajireen? I said: We are looking for these brothers of ours, the Ansar, They said. You should not go near them; do whatever you have already decided, O Muhajireen. I said: By Allah, we will go to them. So we carried on until we came to them in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, where we found them gathered and among them was a man wrapped up [in a garment. I said: Who is this? They said: Saʿd bin ʿUbadah. ! said: What is the matter with him? They said: He is sick. After we sat down, their spokesman stood up and praised and glorified Allah, may He glorified and exalted, as He deserves, then he said: To proceed. We are the supporters (Ansar) of Allah and the majority of the Muslim army. You, O Muhajireen, are a small group among us. Some of you came to us, wanting to deny who we are and prevent us from attaining a position of authority. When he fell silent, I wanted to present a speech that I had prepared and that I liked in front of Abu Bakr ؓ I used to avoid provoking him and he was more forbearing and more dignified than me. But Abu Bakr ؓ said: Wait a while. I did not like to make him angry, and he was more knowledgeable and more dignified than me. By Allah, he did not omit any word that I liked in the speech I had prepared but he said something like it or better, speaking spontaneously, until he finished speaking. Then he said: To proceed. Whatever you have mentioned about your achievements and virtues, is correct. The Arabs would not acknowledge the leadership of anyone except someone from this tribe of Quraish, for they are the best of the Arabs in lineage and location. I am pleased to suggest to you one of these two men, whichever of them you want. Then he took hold of my hand and the hand of Abu ʿUbaidah bin al-Jarrah, and I disliked nothing of what he had said apart from this, for by Allah, I would rather have my neck struck for no sin on my part than to become the leader of people among whom was Abu Bakr ؓ unless my own self suggested something at the time of death. One of the Ansar said: I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree [i.e., a noble]. [I suggest] a ruler from among us and a ruler from among you, O Quraish. - I the narrator said to Malik; What does ‘I am the post on which the cainc! with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm treeʿ mean? He said:It is as if he is saying, I am the smart one who has the answer. - Then there was a great deal of clamour and raised voices, to such an extent that I feared there would be a conflict, so I said: Hold out your hand, O Abu Bakr. So he held out his hand and I swore allegiance to him, and the Muhajireen swore allegiance to him, then the Ansar swore allegiance to him. Thus we surrounded Saʿd bin ‘Ubadah. One of them said: You have killed Saʿd i said: May Allah kill Sa’d! And ʿUmar ؓ said: By Allah, we never encountered any problem greater than the swearing of allegiance to Abu Bakr ؓ . We were afraid that if we left the people without having sworn allegiance to anyone, they might swear allegiance after we were gone, so we would either follow in their footsteps and swear allegiance to someone we were not pleased with, or we would disagree with them and that would cause trouble. If anyone swears allegiance to a leader without consulting the Muslims, there is no allegiance for him and no allegiance to the one who swore allegiance to him, lest both of them be killed. Malik said: Ibn Shihab told me, from ʿUrwah bin az-Zubair, that the men whom they met were ʿUwaim bin Saʿidah and Maʿn bin ʿAdiyy. Ibn Shihab said. Saʿeed bin al-Musayyab told me that the one who said, I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree, was al-lubab bin al-Mundhir. (Using translation from Aḥmad 391)"
"414","I used to recite to ‘AbdurRahman bin ‘Awf, and he found me waiting for him. That was in Mina during the last Hajj performed by ʿUmar bin al-Khattab ؓ Abdur-Rahman bin ʿAwf said: A man came to ʿUmar bin al-Khattab and said: So and so is saying: If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I will swear allegiance to So and so. ʼUmar ؓ said: I will stand before the people today and warn them against these people who want to deprive them of their rights, ʿAbdur-Rahman said: I said: O Ameer al-Muʿmineen, do not do that, for the Hajj season brings together the riffraff and rabble among the people, and most of the people who gather around and listen to you will be of that type. Is you stand before the people, I am afraid that you will say something that they will spread and not understand it properly or interpret it properly. Rather wait until you come to Madinah, for it is the land of Hijrah and the Sunnah, and you will meet the most knowledgeable and noble people there, and you can say what you want to say with confidence; they wilt understand what you say and will interpret it correctly, ʿUmar ؓ said: If I reach Madinah safe and sound, I shall certainly talk to the people there in the first speech I deliver. When we came to Madinah at the end of Dhul-I-Iijah, it was a Friday. I set out early, ‘Umar did not care at what time he went out, because he did not pay attention to heat and cold and so on. I found Saʿeed bin Zaid at the right-hand corner of the minbar, he had got there before me. I sat down next to him, with my knee touching his knee, and it was not long before ʿUmar ؓ came. When I saw him, I said: He will certainly speak today on this minbar and say something that no one ever heard before. Saʿeed bin Zaid objected to that and said: What do you think he will say that no one said before? ʿUmar ؓ sat on the minbar, and when the muʿdhdhin fell silent, he stood up and praised and glorified Allah as He deserves, then he said: To proceed o people, I am going to tell you something that it has been decreed I should say. I do not know, perhaps it may signal my death. So whoever understands it and remembers it, let him narrate it to others wherever his mount takes him; whoever does not understand il, it is not permissible for him to tell lies about me. Allah, may He be blessed and exalted, sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth and revealed the Book to him; among the things that were revealed to him was the verse of stoning [adulterers). We read it and understood it; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned [adulterers] and we stoned adulterers] after him. But I fear that with the passage of time, some people will say: We do not find the verse of stoning in the Book of Allah, thus they will go astray by forsaking an obligation that Allah revealed. Stoning is the due punishment in the Book of Allah for those who commit zina, both men and women, if they have been married and if proof is established, or there is a pregnancy or a confession, And we used to recite: Do not claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, as it is disbelief (or ingratitude) on your part to claim to be the offspring of anyone other than your fathers, Verily the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿDo not praise me excessively as ʿEesa, the son of Maryam, was praised; rather I am the slave of Allah, so say, the slave of Allah and His Messenger.ʿ I have heard that some among you are saying. If ʿUmar ؓ dies, I shall swear allegiance to So and so. No man should deceive himself by saying that the oath of allegiance to Abu Bakr was given suddenly and it was is successful. There is no doubt that this is the case, but Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, saved the to 2 people from its bad consequences and there is no one among you today who has the qualities of Abu Bakr ؓ What happened to us when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died was that ‘Ali, az-Zubair and those who were with them stayed behind in the house of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and all the Ansar stayed behind and gathered in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, whilst the Muhajireen gathered around Abu Bakr ؓ I said to him; O Abu Bakr, let us go to our brothers, the Ansar. So we set out, looking for them, then we were met by two righteous men who told us what the people had done, and said: where are you going, O Muhajireen? I said: We are looking for these brothers of ours, the Ansar, They said. You should not go near them; do whatever you have already decided, O Muhajireen. I said: By Allah, we will go to them. So we carried on until we came to them in Saqeefat Banu Saʿidah, where we found them gathered and among them was a man wrapped up [in a garment. I said: Who is this? They said: Saʿd bin ʿUbadah. ! said: What is the matter with him? They said: He is sick. After we sat down, their spokesman stood up and praised and glorified Allah, may He glorified and exalted, as He deserves, then he said: To proceed. We are the supporters (Ansar) of Allah and the majority of the Muslim army. You, O Muhajireen, are a small group among us. Some of you came to us, wanting to deny who we are and prevent us from attaining a position of authority. When he fell silent, I wanted to present a speech that I had prepared and that I liked in front of Abu Bakr ؓ I used to avoid provoking him and he was more forbearing and more dignified than me. But Abu Bakr ؓ said: Wait a while. I did not like to make him angry, and he was more knowledgeable and more dignified than me. By Allah, he did not omit any word that I liked in the speech I had prepared but he said something like it or better, speaking spontaneously, until he finished speaking. Then he said: To proceed. Whatever you have mentioned about your achievements and virtues, is correct. The Arabs would not acknowledge the leadership of anyone except someone from this tribe of Quraish, for they are the best of the Arabs in lineage and location. I am pleased to suggest to you one of these two men, whichever of them you want. Then he took hold of my hand and the hand of Abu ʿUbaidah bin al-Jarrah, and I disliked nothing of what he had said apart from this, for by Allah, I would rather have my neck struck for no sin on my part than to become the leader of people among whom was Abu Bakr ؓ unless my own self suggested something at the time of death. One of the Ansar said: I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree [i.e., a noble]. [I suggest] a ruler from among us and a ruler from among you, O Quraish. - I the narrator said to Malik; What does ‘I am the post on which the cainc! with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm treeʿ mean? He said:It is as if he is saying, I am the smart one who has the answer. - Then there was a great deal of clamour and raised voices, to such an extent that I feared there would be a conflict, so I said: Hold out your hand, O Abu Bakr. So he held out his hand and I swore allegiance to him, and the Muhajireen swore allegiance to him, then the Ansar swore allegiance to him. Thus we surrounded Saʿd bin ‘Ubadah. One of them said: You have killed Saʿd i said: May Allah kill Sa’d! And ʿUmar ؓ said: By Allah, we never encountered any problem greater than the swearing of allegiance to Abu Bakr ؓ . We were afraid that if we left the people without having sworn allegiance to anyone, they might swear allegiance after we were gone, so we would either follow in their footsteps and swear allegiance to someone we were not pleased with, or we would disagree with them and that would cause trouble. If anyone swears allegiance to a leader without consulting the Muslims, there is no allegiance for him and no allegiance to the one who swore allegiance to him, lest both of them be killed. Malik said: Ibn Shihab told me, from ʿUrwah bin az-Zubair, that the men whom they met were ʿUwaim bin Saʿidah and Maʿn bin ʿAdiyy. Ibn Shihab said. Saʿeed bin al-Musayyab told me that the one who said, I am the post on which the camel with a skin disease scratches itself and I am like a high class palm tree, was al-lubab bin al-Mundhir. (Using translation from Aḥmad 391)"
"415","Both of my ears heard the Messenger of Allah saying this: He who claimed the fatherhood of anyone else besides his real father knowingly (committed a great sin) ;Paradise is forbidden to him. Abu Bakra asserted that he too heard it from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him ). (Using translation from Muslim 63a)"
"416","The narrator says: I mentioned this to Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: I also heard this with my own two ears, and my heart preserved it after hearing it from the tongue of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"417","“Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father, or (a freed slave) who claims that his Wala is for other than his real master, the curse of Allah (SWT), the angels and all the people will be upon him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2609)"
"418","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Yes! Pray for mercy for them, pray for their forgiveness, and fulfill the promises they made after them. Honor their friends, take care of the rights of their relatives—those relatives with whom your relationship exists only because of them. That man said: O Messenger of Allah! How excellent and wonderful this is. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Act upon this."
"419","A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I came to you to take the oath of allegiance to you on emigration, and I left my parents weeping. He (the Prophet) said: Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2528)"
"420","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: Do you have parents? He replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Then serve both of them wholeheartedly."
"421","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Do you have parents?"" He replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Go and treat them well."" So the man left, even though he had come holding his stirrup."
"422","A man emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Yemen. He asked (him): Have you anyone (of your relatives) in the Yemen? He replied: My parents. He asked: Did they permit you? He replied: No. He said: Go back to them and ask for their permission. If they permit you, then fight (in the path of Allah), otherwise be devoted to them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2530)"
"423","""I have come pledging to emigrate (Hijrah), and I have left my parents weeping."" He said: ""Go back to them, and make them smile as you made them weep."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4163)"
"424","A son does not repay what he owes to his father unless he buys him and emancipates him if he finds him in slavery. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5137)"
"425","The father is the middle gate of the gates of Paradise; now if you wish, protect it, and if you wish, leave it."" The narrator says: I think the narrator named Ata stated this: Then that man divorced the woman."
"426","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not like that woman. He instructed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) to divorce that woman. He mentioned this matter to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Obey your father."
"427","A woman was my wife and I loved her, but Umar hated her. He said to me: Divorce her, but I refused. Umar then went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Prophet ﷺ said: Divorce her. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5138)"
"428","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No. Treat your father well and serve him. Abu Kabsha was the maternal grandfather of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). He had traveled to Syria. He liked the religion of the Christians, and when he returned to the Quraysh, he began to preach Christianity. The Quraysh became displeased with him because he was presenting a religion different from theirs. That is why the Quraysh used to taunt the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) in reference to him and attributed him to Abu Kabsha. By this, the Quraysh meant that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had also brought a new religion different from that of those people, just as Abu Kabsha had brought a religion different from theirs."
"429","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The pleasure of Allah is in the pleasure of the father, and the displeasure of Allah is in the displeasure of the father.”"
"430","the Prophet said: ""Among the most dutiful of deeds is that a man nurture relations with the people his father was friends with."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1903)"
"431","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Indeed, the best act of goodness is that a person treats the family of his father's friend well after he (the father) has passed away."
"432","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) came to me. He asked: Do you know why I have come to you? I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever wishes to treat his father well in his grave, he should treat his father's brothers well after his father."" (Ibn Umar said) There was brotherhood and friendship between my father, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and your father, so I wish to treat you well in this regard."
"433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Your mother. He asked: Then who? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Your mother. He asked: Then who? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Your father. The narrator says: The scholars are of the opinion that two-thirds of good treatment should be given to the mother."
"434","Who among the people is most deserving of a fine treatment from my hand? He said: Your mother. He again said: Then who (is the next one)? He said: Again it is your mother (who deserves the best treatment from you). He said: Then who (is the next one)? He (the Holy Prophet) said: Again, it is your mother. He (again) said: Then who? Thereupon he said: Then it is your father. In the hadith transmitted on the authority of Qutalba, there is no mention of the word"" the people"". (Using translation from Muslim 2548a)"
"435","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked him: Are your parents alive? He replied: No. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: Do you have a maternal aunt? He replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Then treat her well."
"436","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said during his illness (before passing away): ""Take care of the rights of your relatives, take care of the rights of your relatives."
"437","The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at the faces of his companions and stopped his camel. He said: This person has been granted success. (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) He has been guided. Do not associate anyone with Allah, perform the prayer, pay the zakat, maintain the ties of kinship, and (now) let go of the camel."
"438","Anyone who is pleased that his sustenance is expanded and his age extended should do kindness to his near relatives. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1693)"
